Add the shared Remote Query runtime for the Postgres and ClickHouse integrations: request contracts, producer diagnostics, bounded source-page uploads, and an intake upload client addressing sessions by upload_id with the org API and application keys, answering page handoffs on 202 acceptance receipts, bounding upload retries by the run-wide deadline, finalizing with bounded pending polling, stamping every page with the agent-reported hostname under the RFC contract_version 1.0.0 format (run id serialized as crawl_id, bare data array, no batch_index in the body), carrying producer execution diagnostics on final and error events, and propagating the Agent trace context as distributed-tracing headers on every upload request. When ddtrace (bundled with the Agent) is importable, admitted runs also emit native producer spans on the supported global tracer: a root span parented on the Agent-supplied trace context carrying run identity, bounded counters, and the terminal status, phase spans for database setup, fetch, encode/page build, finalize, and abort, one span per page-upload attempt with retry classification, and the active span context injected into the page, finalize, and abort request headers in place of the manual trace headers, all fail-open so tracing can never alter a run.